<ContentLayout
  title="SEO Audit Services for Agencies: Scope and Delivery"
  description="Add remote SEO audit capacity for a defined client scope. Confirm branding, evidence, deliverables and timing before work begins. Audits start at $297 USD."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  schema={schema}
  showLeadForm={true}
  publishDate="2026-08-26"
  updateDate="2026-09-11"
>
<p>AuditWeb can provide remote SEO audit capacity for an agency's defined client project. The agreement must state the pages, search questions, available data, report format, branding and communication boundaries.</p>
<p>This service covers diagnosis and recommendations. White-label presentation, implementation support, client contact and recurring capacity are options to confirm during scoping rather than automatic inclusions.</p>

<span id="what-agencies-get" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="agency-scope">What does an agency SEO audit cover?</h2>
<p>An agency SEO audit can examine crawl access, indexing evidence, internal links, on-page targeting, content duplication and agreed competitive questions. The report records affected URLs, evidence, recommended changes and verification steps.</p>
<p>Google separates crawling, rendering and indexing in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/javascript/javascript-seo-basics">JavaScript SEO documentation</a>. Agency reports should identify the observed stage instead of treating every crawl warning as an indexing failure.</p>
<p>Choose the broader <a href="/website-audit-services/agencies/">website audit service for agencies</a> when the client also needs experience, accessibility or public security checks.</p>

<span id="two-ways-to-work-with-us" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="how-white-label-delivery-works" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2 id="delivery-options">Which delivery model fits the agency?</h2>
<p>Choose a full audit when the agency needs an independent investigation. Choose a review when the agency already has findings and wants evidence, scope and priorities checked before client delivery.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Agency-branded report:</strong> provide the approved template and wording rules. Confirm editable format and attribution in writing.</li>
  <li><strong>Internal technical report:</strong> keep source notes and limitations for the agency team to adapt.</li>
  <li><strong>Second review:</strong> supply the existing report, source exports and questions that need verification.</li>
</ul>
<p>AuditWeb does not contact a client or present work as the agency unless the engagement explicitly authorises that arrangement.</p>

<h2 id="required-inputs">What should the agency provide?</h2>
<p>Provide the client domain, business question, priority templates, known changes and named search competitors. Add read-only Search Console or analytics access only when the client has authorised it.</p>
<p>State confidentiality requirements and data-retention rules before sharing exports. Keep passwords and private credentials out of the enquiry form.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">How is an agency engagement priced?</h2>
<p>Basic audits start at $297 USD. Comprehensive audits start at $997 USD. Multi-site, enterprise, recurring and custom-branded work is quoted after scope review.</p>
<p>The quote should name the number of sites, page sample, data sources, deliverable format, revision terms and delivery date. AuditWeb does not publish unverified volume discounts or guaranteed turnaround times.</p>

<h2 id="faq">What should agencies confirm before ordering?</h2>
<h3>Is every report white-label?</h3>
<p>No. White-label delivery is available only when branding and format are agreed in the scope.</p>
<h3>Can AuditWeb review an existing agency audit?</h3>
<p>Yes. Supply the report and supporting evidence. AuditWeb can check whether conclusions follow from that evidence and identify gaps within an agreed review scope.</p>
<h3>Does the service include implementation?</h3>
<p>No. Implementation and follow-up verification require a separate written scope.</p>
</ContentLayout>
